 `CustomerRepository` deliberately behaves like a real paged backend: it refuses
 to return more than `MAX_PAGE_SIZE` (200) rows in a single call. Callers page.

+## Filtering
+
+The list can be narrowed by name and by status. Both are applied by the backend,
+so the grid stays lazy: one page of rows and one count query per filter change,
+whatever the filter matches. A name filter matches when every whitespace-separated
+term occurs in the first or the last name, ignoring case and accents (`makinen`
+finds `Mäkinen`).
+
+The filter is part of the view's URL — `/?name=vir&status=ACTIVE,CLOSED` — so a
+narrowed list survives a reload and can be sent to someone else. Typing rewrites
+the current history entry rather than pushing a new one.
+
